{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2be017f-5e49-5ecf-9256-9026e1e49309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463754} {:answer/id #uuid "64657d11-388e-5eea-8953-1183ad80b2a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463755}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463755} :answer-field/id #uuid "7df1ad99-8fc0-5931-8c43-c2f5f1f4ae55" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183285c5-ecf3-5b1b-a709-43802b2d5542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463756} {:answer/id #uuid "d06d9b80-8f1e-5a1e-92a5-1af63957f4d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463757}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463756} :answer-field/id #uuid "42b05519-bc6b-5846-bb0a-d39f6aaa1a8f" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464812} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b18bdf6-939a-51c6-93bc-947f0d9b20e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463758} {:answer/id #uuid "a14bc920-ef18-5bb6-a154-ff32ab552a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463759}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463758} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ef8c8f-928a-51da-a3d5-e1b9fb740fb3" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "842b19e0-4a35-57fa-95ff-d59ed695ed85" :question/math-academy-id "q-129233" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}9 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}9 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is **not** in row echelon form."}
